(825399, 91985, 21362, '<td valign="top">Oh wow, I totally understood this one and thought it would rank so much higher. I thought it was a great take on the concept of balance!</td>', 'Oh wow, I totally understood this one and thought it would rank so much higher. I thought it was a great take on the concept of balance!', '2004-07-26 01:30:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(825408, 91281, 19952, '<td valign="top">Every challenge, there are a couple of pictures that I rank completely out of line with the rest of the voters. This is one from the current challenge. I absolutely love this shot. It has a very unique style, as if Manet painted a Toulouse-Lautrec subject. Great job!</td>', 'Every challenge, there are a couple of pictures that I rank completely out of line with the rest of the voters. This is one from the current challenge. I absolutely love this shot. It has a very unique style, as if Manet painted a Toulouse-Lautrec subject. Great job!', '2004-07-26 01:34:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(825424, 91033, 21714, '<td valign="top">Excellent work, Dan. CONGRATULATIONS.</td>', 'Excellent work, Dan. CONGRATULATIONS.', '2004-07-26 01:38:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(825432, 91033, 11078, '<td valign="top">Wow! what a neat image. I didnt vote on this challenge but I just love the detail colour and idea well done on your ribbon</td>', 'Wow! what a neat image. I didnt vote on this challenge but I just love the detail colour and idea well done on your ribbon', '2004-07-26 01:41:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(825442, 92126, 7322, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by enigmania:</b></div><hr/><i> The composition works well. I have to admit the subject matter makes the image a little difficult to appreciate. I think it would have worked really well as a black and white photo. This would enhance the textures and shapes. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I thought of that but then I thought, "Then you wouldn''t be able to see the bloody eye socket!". Maybe this would have been a good candidate for selective desat? Just kidding!</td>', 'Originally posted by enigmania: The composition works well. I have to admit the subject matter makes the image a little difficult to appreciate. I think it would have worked really well as a black and white photo. This would enhance the textures and shapes.   I thought of that but then I thought, "Then you wouldn''t be able to see the bloody eye socket!". Maybe this would have been a good candidate for selective desat? Just kidding!', '2004-07-26 01:43:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(825445, 91033, 20235, '<td valign="top">Great work! I knew this one would do well. Congratulations on the well deserved win!</td>', 'Great work! I knew this one would do well. Congratulations on the well deserved win!', '2004-07-26 01:44:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(825453, 91366, 20235, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon! Very beautiful photo : )</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon! Very beautiful photo : )', '2004-07-26 01:46:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(825456, 91987, 20235, '<td valign="top">Super cool photo. Congrats on the ribbon!!</td>', 'Super cool photo. Congrats on the ribbon!!', '2004-07-26 01:47:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(825465, 91987, 17203, '<td valign="top">Wonderful concept, a funky visual effect, and a great title to tie it all together. Well deserved! You were overdue for a ribbon anyway... it''s been almost three weeks since your last one. Bet you were starting to get a nervous twitch on your shutter finger. ;-)</td>', 'Wonderful concept, a funky visual effect, and a great title to tie it all together. Well deserved! You were overdue for a ribbon anyway... it''s been almost three weeks since your last one. Bet you were starting to get a nervous twitch on your shutter finger. ;-)', '2004-07-26 01:52:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(825466, 91803, 16106, '<td valign="top">Yes,I admit it, I stole the purple cloth from Heida( actually a flannel bed sheet as Keegbow pointed out) because it looked less mystic when I did it in a tee shirt.The whole robed in purple adds that Tolkinesque quality that make sword balancing seem less silly. I can do this balance trick with the sword and there are people who can do the wine glass platter on the sword trick, I''m just not one of them. I made up for this lack of skill by sticking a piece of shelving under the books in a bookshelf and perching the tray with the glasses on it, and hanging the sword on a nail hammered in the end of the board. By draping the whole thing with black fabric it hid the support. Cheap trick, but I kept my glassware intact. The lighting sort of failed but it was fun to do anyway.</td>', 'Yes,I admit it, I stole the purple cloth from Heida( actually a flannel bed sheet as Keegbow pointed out) because it looked less mystic when I did it in a tee shirt.The whole robed in purple adds that Tolkinesque quality that make sword balancing seem less silly. I can do this balance trick with the sword and there are people who can do the wine glass platter on the sword trick, I''m just not one of them. I made up for this lack of skill by sticking a piece of shelving under the books in a bookshelf and perching the tray with the glasses on it, and hanging the sword on a nail hammered in the end of the board. By draping the whole thing with black fabric it hid the support. Cheap trick, but I kept my glassware intact. The lighting sort of failed but it was fun to do anyway.', '2004-07-26 01:52:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(825481, 91033, 17203, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first blue... you definitely earned it.</td>', 'Congrats on your first blue... you definitely earned it.', '2004-07-26 01:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(825505, 92170, 21362, '<td valign="top">You used the same technique I did for mine -- I had daisies and nails holding them up. But my entry feels garish and overdone in comparison to the simple beauty in yours. The detail is nice. Good job!</td>', 'You used the same technique I did for mine -- I had daisies and nails holding them up. But my entry feels garish and overdone in comparison to the simple beauty in yours. The detail is nice. Good job!', '2004-07-26 02:12:33.000000', NULL, 0),
