(827338, 91987, 200, '<td valign="top">I submitted this in color originally...but decided the duotone was even quirckier. Being that the sun was directly above the bride and groom...their faces were rather dark and shadowy. First off....had to remove sensor dust..and boy is it bad. I made a layer of the original image and intensified the contrast...then erased to reveal the original levels of the bride and groom. So much contrast would have completely blown out her dress. I then played with the levels on the original ...to lighten the bride and groom. Played with levels on the layer to increase darkness and contrast. I erased a bit around the water to reveal the original and make for a darker sky. Flattened the layers...dodged a bit of his face and added a vignette around the image. Border. Duotone and more playing with levels and contrast to bring out the detail of the boardwalk. All in all..maybe spent 10 to 15 minutes on it...if that.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-07-27 08:29:57.</i></td>', 'I submitted this in color originally...but decided the duotone was even quirckier. Being that the sun was directly above the bride and groom...their faces were rather dark and shadowy. First off....had to remove sensor dust..and boy is it bad. I made a layer of the original image and intensified the contrast...then erased to reveal the original levels of the bride and groom. So much contrast would have completely blown out her dress. I then played with the levels on the original ...to lighten the bride and groom. Played with levels on the layer to increase darkness and contrast. I erased a bit around the water to reveal the original and make for a darker sky. Flattened the layers...dodged a bit of his face and added a vignette around the image. Border. Duotone and more playing with levels and contrast to bring out the detail of the boardwalk. All in all..maybe spent 10 to 15 minutes on it...if that.', '2004-07-27 09:21:45.000000', '2004-07-27 09:29:57.000000', 0),
