(835816, 91581, 22734, '<td valign="top">From the critique club:<br/>  This shot was composed with the abstract meaning of balance and of course chock full of humor. I loved it and it is obvious the sense of humor was not received well by a small block of voters.<br/> <br/> <br/>  I ask myself the question following this following observation: It is a top notch composition using three persons. A spanking and dashing beautiful classic car with a most outstanding color shade. It is outdoors and it is a very attractive shot. Exposure and selective desaturation done very well. Look at this picture and tell me where 29 voters gave it a 4: 7 gave a 3 and two gave it 2. Am I missing something here. The argument that it may be offensive to woman does not even apply, because the girls are not nude nor are they showing more than they have to and there is no vulgarity whatsoever. This confirms my belief that many voters are not here to learn but to express their strong likes and dislikes irrespective of the quality of the image. I am convinced that these low voters have yet to reach the enlightened realm necessary to become top notch photographers. When you put down ideas and quality work, you trampled the very structure one needs to succeed. Come on, judge the image on quality and composition even if it is of a negative subject. This image is at least a six and if you hate the subject matter you take one off. End of case. <br/> <br/>   Your consolation is that despite these low voters, the image arose to 5.59. The joke is on them, because the majority got the humor and most important appreciated the good quality of this composition. This goes in my favorites. Job well done... dan<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-08-01 22:48:39.</i></td>', 'From the critique club:  This shot was composed with the abstract meaning of balance and of course chock full of humor. I loved it and it is obvious the sense of humor was not received well by a small block of voters.    I ask myself the question following this following observation: It is a top notch composition using three persons. A spanking and dashing beautiful classic car with a most outstanding color shade. It is outdoors and it is a very attractive shot. Exposure and selective desaturation done very well. Look at this picture and tell me where 29 voters gave it a 4: 7 gave a 3 and two gave it 2. Am I missing something here. The argument that it may be offensive to woman does not even apply, because the girls are not nude nor are they showing more than they have to and there is no vulgarity whatsoever. This confirms my belief that many voters are not here to learn but to express their strong likes and dislikes irrespective of the quality of the image. I am convinced that these low voters have yet to reach the enlightened realm necessary to become top notch photographers. When you put down ideas and quality work, you trampled the very structure one needs to succeed. Come on, judge the image on quality and composition even if it is of a negative subject. This image is at least a six and if you hate the subject matter you take one off. End of case.     Your consolation is that despite these low voters, the image arose to 5.59. The joke is on them, because the majority got the humor and most important appreciated the good quality of this composition. This goes in my favorites. Job well done... dan', '2004-08-01 23:22:17.000000', '2004-08-01 23:48:39.000000', 0),
(835817, 92168, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Spanish_Grease:</b></div><hr/><i> Overall, I think your idea had merit.  It was a bit of stretch to fit the challenge, but it did so in a humorous way.  Knowing your work GeneralE, it seems like you were a bit rushed putting this together and couldn''t put everything into it.<br/> <br/>Lee </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I think you summed it up nicely!</td>', 'Originally posted by Spanish_Grease: Overall, I think your idea had merit.  It was a bit of stretch to fit the challenge, but it did so in a humorous way.  Knowing your work GeneralE, it seems like you were a bit rushed putting this together and couldn''t put everything into it. Lee  I think you summed it up nicely!', '2004-08-01 23:23:06.000000', NULL, 0),
